# Dev fixtures for T1-2a browser-dev mode (per ADR-0008).
# These are regenerable from `cargo run --bin dump_frames` and are
# committed-out so the repo doesn't carry 100s of KB of derived JSON.
# Vite serves files in this directory at `/dev-fixtures/...`.
#
# Regenerate the standard smoke fixture:
#
#   cargo run --bin dump_frames -- --seed 0xdeadbeef --ticks 60 > frontend/public/dev-fixtures/smoke.json
#
# Then visit:
#
#   http://localhost:1420/dev/board?source=fixture:/dev-fixtures/smoke.json
*.json
# board-sample.json is intentionally tracked: it's the committed fixture the
# /dev/board-preview harness mounts so the production <TacticalBoard> is
# browser-previewable (and Claude-Preview-MCP screenshottable) with no Tauri
# IPC. Regenerate per the header comment in src/routes/Dev/BoardPreview.tsx.
!board-sample.json
!.gitignore
# T4-I1: IPC-command fixtures for the DEV-ONLY browser fixture backend.
# These are hand-authored static JSON payloads (one per read command) committed
# alongside the shim so `pnpm dev ?backend=fixtures` works out of the box.
# They are NOT regenerable from a bin — they must stay in the repo.
!get_settings.json
!get_squad_roster.json
!get_player_detail.json
!get_scout_report.json
!get_standings.json
!get_fixtures.json
!get_career_overview.json
!get_press_inbox.json
